{"id": "whsikhote", "name": "Central Sikhote-Alin", "short": "Sikhote-Alin", "place": "Primorsky Krai, Russia", "lat": 45.03, "lon": 136.33, "side": "l", "cont": "Asia", "country": "Russia", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Korean pine, wapiti and boar feed the Amur tiger in the Far East forest.", "tip": {"id": "pine", "title": "Remove the Korean pine", "text": "Pine seeds feed boar, bears, sables and nutcrackers. Set Korean pine to -100% and watch those seed eaters, then the tiger that preys on them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Sikhote-Alin Nature Reserve", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sikhote-Alin_Nature_Reserve"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Sikhote-Alin", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sikhote-Alin"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Siberian tiger", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siberian_tiger"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Ussuri brown bear", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ussuri_brown_bear"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Siberian musk deer", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siberian_musk_deer"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Wild boar", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_boar"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Sikhote-Alin Nature Reserve", "icon": "whitebark", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.15, "desc": "Summer light drives growth in the forest canopy and understorey of the mountain slopes."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "summer monsoon rain", "xh": 0.4, "desc": "The Russian Far East gets its rain mostly in the warm season, feeding the lush mixed forest on the coastal slopes."}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "forest soil & nutrients", "xh": 0.65}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.88, "name": "Fungi, bacteria & insects", "desc": "Break down fallen leaves,